.TH TRICKSTER 1 "0.1.0" "trickster 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
trickster \- Flutter-native Wayland status bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trickster
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B trickster
is a Flutter-native Wayland status bar built on
.BR wlr-layer-shell .
It draws one strip surface per connected output and renders the Denial bar
language: floating pill cards for clock, battery, media, system tray,
CPU/GPU meters, and workspaces.
.PP
The bar is a guest of the host compositor. It never owns outputs, input
routing, or composition, and it reserves exactly the strip through its
layer-shell exclusive zone.
.PP
With no options the bar starts normally.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Preflight the session (wayland, configs, layer-shell, outputs) and exit.
Exits non-zero when any check fails.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Use
.I PATH
as the outputs.conf override for this run.
.TP
.BI \-\-edge " SIDE"
One-shot edge override:
.BR top ,
.BR bottom ,
.B left ,
or
.BR right .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TRICKSTER_LAYER
Layer-shell layer: top, bottom, background, or overlay.
.TP
.B TRICKSTER_NAMESPACE
Layer-shell namespace (default: trickster).
.TP
.B TRICKSTER_KEYBOARD
Keyboard interactivity: none, on_demand, or exclusive.
.TP
.B TRICKSTER_ACCENT
Accent color used until settings.json supplies one.
.TP
.B TRICKSTER_LOG
Native logging filter.
.TP
.B TRICKSTER_OUTPUT_CONFIG
Optional outputs.conf override path.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/trickster/session.conf
Machine configuration, packaged as a pacman backup file.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/trickster/outputs.conf
Bar placement; seeded from the packaged template on first launch and
never overwritten afterward.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/trickster/settings.json
Versioned settings document.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/trickster/control.sock
Control socket served to
.BR tricksterctl (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tricksterctl (1)
.SH LICENSE
GPL-3.0-or-later.
